ORES HIPOFISARIOS,\"Los tumores hipofisarios son neoplasias que se desarrollan en la glándula pituitaria y tienen la capacidad de secretar hormonas como la TSH (hormona estimulante de la tiroides) y la GH (hormona de crecimiento), entre otras.\",12\r\n3729,CASANUEVA FF,\"Casanueva FF is an author known for their contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the study of prolactin disorders. They have authored a publication that discusses various aspects of these disorders, with a specific focus on the epidemiology and causes, while excluding prolactin-secreting pituitary tumors. In addition to their work on prolactin disorders, Casanueva FF has also researched hypopituitarism, exploring its treatment options. Furthermore, they have written extensively about pituitary tumors and their management, showcasing a comprehensive understanding of these related conditions within the endocrine system.\",5\r\n3734,CRANEORAFINGIOMAS,\"Craneofaringiomas, also known as craniopharyngiomas, are tumors that can impact the pituitary gland, potentially resulting in hormonal deficiencies such as hypopituitarism. These tumors originate from remnants of Rathke's pouch and account for approximately 1-3% of all brain tumors. They exhibit a bimodal distribution, primarily affecting both children and adults.\",4\r\n3735,SARCOIDOSIS,\"Sarcoidosis is an inflammatory disease that can impact various organs, including the pituitary gland. This condition may lead to several complications, such as diabetes insipidus and hypopituitarism, both of which are related to the dysfunction of the pituitary gland. Additionally, sarcoidosis can cause hypercalcemia, which results from the increased endogenous production of calcitriol. Overall, sarcoidosis presents a range of potential health issues, particularly concerning endocrine function and calcium metabolism.\",3\r\n3770,ADENOMAS,\"Adenomas are non-functioning tumors that primarily occur in the pituitary gland, necessitating close observat